{"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore"]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseActor","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseHandle","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/StatementHandle"],"anchor":"Topics"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/loomcore\/concurrencymodel"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How LoomCore makes SQLite race-free without explicit locking."}],"metadata":{"title":"Concurrency and Actor Isolation","modules":[{"name":"LoomCore"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Articles","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/IndexConventions","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SafeInterpolation","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/StoringCustomTypes","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/QueryingJSON","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FullTextSearch","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionsAndServices"],"anchor":"Articles","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SQLite is thread-safe in the sense that the C library can be configured to serialize access internally, but using it correctly from Swift still requires discipline — prepared statements, transactions, and the connection state are all stateful and must not be touched from multiple threads concurrently."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"LoomCore uses a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"single global actor"}]},{"type":"text","text":" to serialize every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sqlite3_*"},{"type":"text","text":" call:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@globalActor","public actor DatabaseActor {","  public static let shared = DatabaseActor()","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every public method on "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", every static method on "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Bindable","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and every closure passed in ("},{"code":"Binder","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Stepper","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"transaction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s body) is "},{"code":"@DatabaseActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"-isolated. Swift’s compiler enforces this at the call site — you cannot call into LoomCore from arbitrary async code without first hopping to the actor."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"What this guarantees","anchor":"What-this-guarantees"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No two SQLite calls run at the same time, ever, in your process."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No accidental shared mutable state between callers — the actor is the single point of synchronization."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" values you pass into binders and steppers are safe to capture; mutable references are flagged at compile time."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once an operation starts executing, it runs to completion synchronously on the actor. Interleaving between tasks happens only at suspension points — never in the middle of a statement."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"The transaction gate","anchor":"The-transaction-gate"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Actor isolation alone is not enough for transactions: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseActor","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" releases its executor at every "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so a transaction body that suspends would otherwise let another task’s statements run inside the open transaction. LoomCore closes that hole with a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"gate"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While a transaction is in flight — including while its body is suspended — database operations from tasks outside the transaction suspend at the gate and resume once the transaction commits or rolls back. Membership is a task-local token bound around the transaction block: structured children ("},{"code":"async let","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", task groups) and unstructured "},{"code":"Task {}","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" inherit it and run inside the transaction — an unstructured task must complete before the body returns, or it races the commit; "},{"code":"Task.detached","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does not inherit it and waits like any outside caller. An operation waiting at the gate throws "},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if its task is cancelled."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The gate is what makes "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" inside a transaction body safe. When no transaction is active it costs a single nil check. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionsAndServices","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the full semantics, including savepoint nesting."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Cancellation","anchor":"Cancellation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancellation is ambient — no opt-in, no API knob:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Waiting at the gate","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — a cancelled waiter resumes throwing "},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", leaving the in-flight transaction undisturbed."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Mid-statement","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — cancelling a task whose "},{"code":"exec","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"query","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"code":"execScript","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is stepping aborts the statement via "},{"code":"sqlite3_interrupt","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the one SQLite call that is safe cross-thread on a live connection) and throws "},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". This works even inside a single long-running step, and a per-operation ticket guarantees a late-firing cancellation can never abort a different task’s statement."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An interrupted "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"write"}]},{"type":"text","text":" inside an explicit transaction makes SQLite roll the whole transaction back; "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/transaction(kind:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" recognizes that, reports a rollback to services, and leaves the connection open."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/interrupt()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" exposes the same abort switch directly — it is "},{"code":"nonisolated","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so any thread can stop a long query on a busy connection without cancelling the task running it. The interrupted operation throws "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/LoomError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SQLiteResultCode\/interrupt","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/directAccess(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the exception: it runs no LoomCore statements, so nothing is armed — code inside it manages its own cancellation."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"What this rules out","anchor":"What-this-rules-out"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Concurrent reads against the same ","type":"text"},{"code":"Database","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Even if SQLite would allow it (e.g. in WAL mode), LoomCore serializes everything through the actor. If you want true read parallelism, open multiple "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database"},{"type":"text","text":" instances against the same file — each has its own connection and runs on its own actor turn."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cross-actor ","type":"text"},{"code":"StatementHandle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" use.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/StatementHandle"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseHandle"},{"type":"text","text":" are "},{"code":"~Copyable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and isolated to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseActor"},{"type":"text","text":". They cannot escape into other contexts."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Resource cleanup","anchor":"Resource-cleanup"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseHandle","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" owns the "},{"code":"sqlite3*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" pointer plus the prepared-statement cache. It is "},{"code":"~Copyable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to enforce single ownership. Cleanup happens in two ways:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Explicit close","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"db.close()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" finalizes cached statements and closes the connection eagerly."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — the handle dispatches a "},{"code":"Task { @DatabaseActor … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that runs the same cleanup. Because deinit can run on any thread, the cleanup work is moved into a "},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whose body is on "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseActor"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The cache is captured via a small reference-counted "},{"code":"ResourceStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so it survives the move into the cleanup task. You should not normally see this internal structure — it just means resources are released safely without you having to think about it."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Working with SwiftUI and structured concurrency","anchor":"Working-with-SwiftUI-and-structured-concurrency"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Database","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it can be passed across actor boundaries. The methods that mutate it are isolated to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseActor","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct User: Sendable {","  let id: Int","  let name: String","}","","@MainActor","final class UserStore {","  let db: Database","","  init(db: Database) {","    self.db = db","  }","","  func loadUsers() async throws -> [User] {","    try await db.query(\"SELECT id, name FROM users\") { stmt, _ in","      User(","        id: try Int.column(of: stmt, at: 0),","        name: try String.column(of: stmt, at: 1)","      )","    }","  }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the actor hop from "},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseActor","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Results returned to the main actor must be "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ConcurrencyModel","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/SafeInterpolation":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/safeinterpolation","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Safe SQL Interpolation","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SafeInterpolation","abstract":[{"text":"When ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\(value)"},{"text":" becomes a parameter, when it becomes literal text, and how to keep injection-prone surfaces small.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/FullTextSearch":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/fulltextsearch","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Full-Text Search","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FullTextSearch","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Match, rank, and excerpt text with typed expressions over SQLite’s FTS5 extension.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/transaction(kind:_:)":{"type":"topic","title":"transaction(kind:_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"transaction"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TransactionKind","preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore15TransactionKindO"},{"kind":"text","text":", ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Database","preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore8DatabaseC"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"T"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/transaction(kind:_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs a block of operations atomically inside a transaction."}],"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/transaction(kind:_:)"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/LoomError":{"url":"\/docum